- a59 — "esimese astme kohus mõistis välja TWD 1.57M" → "1,57 miljonit TWD". SKIPPED by ACCEPTED-ROUND / R12: "TWD 1.57M" is pinned byte-identical by a test (GUIDANCE_BIO_PINNED_TERMS in src/data/international-guidance-team.ts).
- a40 + b7 — zero-width-space layout damage / restoring "##" headings in 003 and removing U+200B-only lines in 005, 006, 008, 009, 013, 015. SKIPPED as structural: the Korean sources carry exactly the same ZWSP lines and the same missing "##" (003 line 198 is "Q16. …" in ko too), and checkBlocks pins both the block count and the ZWSP count (`ZWSP n → n`). Fixing it means changing the Korean source, which is outside this work order. Counts verified: ko/et ZWSP 52/52 (003), 8/8 (005), 4/4 (006), 10/10 (008), 5/5 (009), 5/5 (013), 3/3 (015).
- a38 (partial) — "iga täidetud 1 staažiaasta" (008, two places: front-matter FAQ + block quote) and "põhimõtteliselt 1 järgmistest kriteeriumidest" (001, two places). REVERTED after the checker failed: the Korean source writes these as digits (근속 1년, 설립 1년 …) and checkNumbers treats a missing source digit as FAIL ("missing from translation (2): 1×2" for 001, "(1): 1" for 008). The other instances of the same row (002 "ühel kontol", "ühe teatega"; 018 "üks või kaks juhatajat") were applied and pass.
- a39 (partial) — wrote "iga 2 kuu tagant" rather than the reviewer's "iga kahe kuu tagant": the postposition (the actual defect) is fixed, the digit kept because the ko source has 2개월.
- b18 (variant) — "25. juunil 2026" fails the checker: DATE_MONTH_NAMES only lists nominative Estonian month names ("juuni"), so the adessive hides the month digit 6 and the number gate reports "missing from translation (1): 6". Used the checker-safe, still-grammatical "seisuga 25. juuni 2026".
- b6 (variant) — same cause: "Alates 1. juulist 2026" produced "missing from translation (3): 7×3". Used "Alates kuupäevast 1. juuli 2026" (3 instances), which is grammatical Estonian officialese and keeps the month name in the parsed form.

